# Routes review by path. GitHub auto-requests review from the owner listed here
# whenever a PR touches one of these files.
#
# Read docs/WORKFLOW.md before relying on this as a gate: on a single-owner
# repository CODEOWNERS cannot mechanically block a merge, because GitHub does
# not let an author approve their own pull request. What it does reliably is
# make a tier 3 change visible as a tier 3 change.

# Default: everything is the owner's, so nothing lands unnoticed.
*                           @aidiaz

# Tier 3 — authorisation, secrets, deployment, and the CI that gates the rest.
/src/soma/serve/oauth.py @aidiaz
/src/soma/config.py      @aidiaz
/.github/                   @aidiaz
/deploy/                    @aidiaz
/compose.pi.yaml            @aidiaz
/Dockerfile                 @aidiaz
/.env.example               @aidiaz

# The rules an agent works under. Changing these changes every future PR, so it
# is treated as tier 3 even though it ships no code.
/CLAUDE.md                  @aidiaz
/docs/WORKFLOW.md           @aidiaz
